  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Simplify $\\displaystyle\\frac{5^{3x+1}-5^{3x-1}+24}{24\\times5^{3x}+120}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{5}$\n\nFactor the numerator and denominator to reveal their common factor.",
      "worked": "Let $t=5^{3x-1}$, so $5^{3x}=5t$ and $5^{3x+1}=25t$. Let $E$ denote the given expression.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=\\frac{25t-t+24}{120t+120}\\\\E&=\\frac{24t+24}{120t+120}\\\\E&=\\frac{24(t+1)}{120(t+1)}\\\\E&=\\frac{1}{5}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $t>0$, the cancelled factor $t+1$ is non-zero.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
